Here is the printable daily routine sheet:

<%= "#{ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST}/routine_sheet" %>

Open it and print it — one page, big type, room for medication times, meals
and the phone numbers worth having on the fridge door.

In case you haven't looked yet: Remindly rings your parent's own phone,
landline or mobile, when something is due (tablets, a glass of water, an
appointment) and says it out loud. They press 1 when it's done. If there's a
tablet in the house, it can speak from the screen instead. You set it all up
from wherever you are, and for medication you get an email when a dose is
marked done, or when the time passes and nobody marks it.

It's free while in beta:
<%= "#{ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST}/?from=welcome-email" %>

Or watch the 11-minute walk-through:
<%= "#{ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST}/how_to?from=welcome-email#videos" %>

About once a month I send one useful thing about caring for a parent at a
distance, and a line on what has changed in Remindly. That is all — no more
than that. Unsubscribe any time:

<%= "#{ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST}/subscribers/unsubscribe/#{@subscriber.signed_id(purpose: :unsubscribe)}" %>

Or just reply to this email to stop.
